---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Native capture-preserving syntax template, not literal replacement text

Usage: pse propose syntax [OPTIONS] --pattern <PATTERN> --replacement <REPLACEMENT> <FILES>...

Arguments:
  <FILES>...  Exact source operands, acquired independently without a semantic session

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --pattern <PATTERN>          Native code-shaped Rust pattern ($NAME or $$$SEQUENCE captures)
      --format <FORMAT>            Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --strictness <STRICTNESS>    [default: smart] [possible values: cst, smart, ast, relaxed, signature, template]
      --fields <FIELDS>            Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage
      --inside <INSIDE>            Require an ancestor matching each native pattern
      --budget <BUDGET>            Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --has <HAS>                  Require a proper descendant matching each native pattern
      --exclude <EXCLUDE>          Exclude a candidate matching any of these native patterns
      --capture <CAPTURE>          Extract only this named capture (without sigils); absence retains all captures
      --index                      Read the raw staging-index blob rather than working bytes
      --revision <REVISION>        Read a committed blob; resolve the revision before returning its identity
      --language <LANGUAGE>        Override the .rs/.md/.markdown filename inference [possible values: rust, markdown]
      --edition <EDITION>          Explicit syntax policy; no Cargo edition or cfg discovery is performed [default: 2024] [possible values: 2015, 2018, 2021, 2024]
      --replacement <REPLACEMENT>
      --select <SELECTED>          Select candidate indices; absence retains candidates without choosing edits
  -h, --help                       Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Native capture-preserving syntax template, not literal replacement text

Usage: pse propose syntax [OPTIONS] --pattern <PATTERN> --replacement <REPLACEMENT> <FILES>...

Arguments:
  <FILES>...
          Exact source operands, acquired independently without a semantic session

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --pattern <PATTERN>
          Native code-shaped Rust pattern ($NAME or $$$SEQUENCE captures)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --strictness <STRICTNESS>
          Possible values:
          - cst:       Match all concrete syntax nodes
          - smart:     Native smart policy, retaining significant written syntax
          - ast:       Match named AST nodes
          - relaxed:   Ignore comments and unnamed punctuation
          - signature: Compare structural signatures without terminal text
          - template:  Native textual template matching policy

          [default: smart]

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage

      --inside <INSIDE>
          Require an ancestor matching each native pattern

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --has <HAS>
          Require a proper descendant matching each native pattern

      --exclude <EXCLUDE>
          Exclude a candidate matching any of these native patterns

      --capture <CAPTURE>
          Extract only this named capture (without sigils); absence retains all captures

      --index
          Read the raw staging-index blob rather than working bytes

      --revision <REVISION>
          Read a committed blob; resolve the revision before returning its identity

      --language <LANGUAGE>
          Override the .rs/.md/.markdown filename inference

          Possible values:
          - rust:     Lossless Rust syntax, without Cargo/cfg/macro expansion
          - markdown: CommonMark headings and their source sections

      --edition <EDITION>
          Explicit syntax policy; no Cargo edition or cfg discovery is performed

          Possible values:
          - 2015: Rust 2015 syntax
          - 2018: Rust 2018 syntax
          - 2021: Rust 2021 syntax
          - 2024: Rust 2024 syntax

          [default: 2024]

      --replacement <REPLACEMENT>


      --select <SELECTED>
          Select candidate indices; absence retains candidates without choosing edits

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
